WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.173
- [Mark] All right, Leanna.

00:00:10.173 --> 00:00:11.530
Leanna, where are you from originally?

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.363
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:12.363 --> 00:00:14.310
- Montana
- [Mark] What city?

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:15.740
- In Missoula area.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.573
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood,

00:00:16.573 --> 00:00:18.380
you grew up with both your parents?

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.820
- [Leanna] No, I was
actually abused until...

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.810
and I lived with my mom and dad,

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.610
for a little bit on and
off, and foster care

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.190
and then about seven

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.653
I was put into permanent foster care,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.887
for three years, I lived
next to a guy who finally

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.340
became the governor of Montana

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:47.863
and then moved to
Missoula to a foster home,

00:00:47.863 --> 00:00:50.783
till I was 20 at the age of 10 and a half.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.580
- [Mark] So you left your
biological parents at what age?

00:00:58.235 --> 00:01:00.560
- Officially about five or six,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.790
that I finally couldn't
live with them anymore.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.890
- [Mark] What was going
on that they lost you?

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.780
- My dad was abusive

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.780
and my mom was in and out
of the BHU Mental Hospital,

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.540
from the abuse.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.170
- [Mark] Oh, he was
abusing your mom as well?

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.073
- Mmhmm, and my sister
- [Mark] And your sister.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.410
How was your childhood in general?

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:26.643
- It was rough.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.770
- [Mark] You were bounced around?

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.793
- I couldn't be who I was inside,

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:36.360
being trans in Montana,

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.700
would have probably gotten me killed

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.543
and I just didn't really
have a happy childhood.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.990
- [Mark] You left home at what age?

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:49.090
- 19, I left the foster family,

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.963
actually, I said 20 but it was 19,

00:01:55.622 --> 00:01:59.480
I tried working on and off up until 2006,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.283
when I finally got my social security,

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.670
couldn't really hold a job that much,

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.443
because of my mental illness,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.890
I was homeless quite a bit.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.380
I actually got into a
really good apartment,

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:23.380
before I came here and gave
that up for my transition.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.080
- [Mark] So you made the
transition from male to--

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:28.913
- Female.

00:02:28.913 --> 00:02:29.860
- [Mark] At what age?

00:02:32.761 --> 00:02:35.580
- I was 40 and a half
years old when I came out.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:36.640
- [Mark] Oh, and how old are you now?

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:37.730
- 44.
- [Mark] Okay,

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.830
so this is fairly recent?
- Yeah.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.790
- [Mark] So you lived all
your life mostly as a man,

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:43.890
kind of in hiding?

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.100
- In hiding, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.910
- [Mark] In Montana you have to, right?

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:48.743
- Yeah.

00:02:51.966 --> 00:02:53.063
- [Mark] They don't accept that, right?

00:02:53.063 --> 00:02:53.896
- When I was in high school,

00:02:53.896 --> 00:02:56.400
- [Mark] Especially when you were young--

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.400
- There was a famous case in Wyoming,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.500
where a gay guy or gay kid got killed.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:03.733
- [Mark] Yeah, I remember that.

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:09.463
- And so, I couldn't, I
knew I couldn't come out,

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:14.730
I struggled with it even
when I came out in 2016,

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.393
because it's still not
tolerated much, sir.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.883
I made the choice to
start trying to be happy,

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.153
no matter what everybody else thinks.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.090
- [Mark] At what point did you come to LA?

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:33.850
- I came here back in,

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:38.740
two years ago, in
February or March of 2019.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:46.160
I wasn't expecting quite so
much hate, being an LGBT state.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.630
I came here because it's one of the States

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:54.630
that does many mighty
for finishing transition

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.660
and I've been homeless ever since,

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.043
but I'm getting closer
to getting my house.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.050
- [Mark] In terms of transition,
are you saying medically?

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.437
- Medically.
- [Mark] What have you done?

00:04:09.437 --> 00:04:11.570
- I've been wanting to do surgeries,

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:14.280
but I can't have it until
I have my own place.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:15.230
- [Mark] Oh, I see.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.950
- There's a few different
surgeries that I'm wanting.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:19.783
- [Mark] Sure, there are.

00:04:19.783 --> 00:04:20.903
- Bottom surgery,

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.980
the Adam's apple and possibly voice.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.711
- [Mark] Is that right?
- Right.

00:04:30.711 --> 00:04:33.380
- [Mark] I know that a lot of
the ladies take hormones too.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:38.380
- Yeah, I've been on those
since January 27th of 2017.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.010
- [Mark] You're happier as a female?

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.410
- Yeah, I'm a lot happier.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.020
- [Mark] That's great.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.120
Where do you live now?

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.273
- I'm at a shelter off of Central Avenue.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.240
- [Mark] So you're in Skid Row or?

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.823
- No, I'm almost,

00:04:59.668 --> 00:05:02.580
I'm a few blocks past Vernon Avenue.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.930
- [Mark] Oh, so you're not
really nearby Skid Row.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.550
- No, I come here, hang out

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.773
at the Women's Center and
visit some of my friends but,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.020
after

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.900
some hassle at Midnight Mission,

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.910
I've been trying to stay
out of Skid Row area.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.750
- [Mark] You used to live here?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:25.750
- I had a bad hate crime
happen on 5th and San Julian.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.960
- [Mark] What happened?
- A week before Christmas,

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.360
a guy, because I was transgender hit me

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.023
with a metal folding chair several times,

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:39.100
broke my cane on me, hit me with fists,

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.090
and

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.713
I am still suffering a concussion from it.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.830
- [Mark] So you used to
live on the street here?

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:52.270
- Yeah, I've had tons of hate crime.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.253
I've been beat up several
times, almost burnt alive,

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.360
right outside of the Women's Center

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.110
where I slept on the street.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.760
- [Mark] Somebody put you
on, set you're on fire?

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.920
- [Leanna] They doused
my sleeping bag with...

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.250
I woke up a few seconds later
with the zipper tampered with

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.400
and it's soaked with lighter fluid,

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.453
so many had chased him off.

00:06:14.479 --> 00:06:16.325
- [Mark] Oh my God,

00:06:16.325 --> 00:06:17.423
that's horrible.

00:06:17.423 --> 00:06:20.823
- [Leanna] That was like
September 2nd, of 2019.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:23.583
- [Mark] Wow.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:28.630
So you're in a shelter right
now, that you feel safer in?

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:29.463
- [Leanna] Yeah.

00:06:37.327 --> 00:06:40.360
One of the most dangerous
parts of LA for trans,

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.410
is right in the Skid Row area.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:45.420
- [Mark] I'm sure there's
lots of violent crime here--

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.220
- [Leanna] There's lots of resources

00:06:48.273 --> 00:06:49.963
and that's where most of us come.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.290
- [Mark] Do you have friends?

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:57.360
- [Leanna] I have a few friends

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.053
at the downtown Women's Center,

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.220
I just got out of a
relationship with my ex

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:10.220
and anytime I made friends, I
don't have that many because,

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:15.340
my ex made me cut ties with
anybody I made friends with.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.990
- [Mark] What do you do for money now?

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:24.370
- I'm on Social Security Disability,

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:27.223
but it's just not enough
to live off really.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.783
- [Mark] Are there any other
options for you to make money?

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:34.843
- With my physical disabilities
and stuff, it's hard.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.643
There's a few things I can do,

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.493
I just haven't gotten into doing it.

00:07:46.544 --> 00:07:48.344
- [Mark] What are your disabilities?

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:54.210
- I have a real bad knee,
bad ankles, bad balance

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:58.363
and a severe bad back,
I fractured it one time,

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.640
been in multiple accidents,

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.980
along with degenerative disc, bulging disc

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:05.813
and

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.190
narrowing of the spine.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:11.040
- [Mark] And you also mentioned mental?

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.200
- Yes, I have bipolar one,

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:18.550
ADHD, manic depression

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:20.900
and the manic depression
is the worst of it,

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.963
it makes it hard to hold a job.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.240
- [Mark] I'm sure.

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:26.750
What do you wish was different
about your childhood,

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.550
that may have made your life easier?

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:34.523
- I just wish that there was more love,

00:08:41.266 --> 00:08:42.740
I wish it was like today

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:45.570
when trans are able to
come out to their parents

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:50.418
and live the life that they wanna live,

00:08:50.418 --> 00:08:54.430
instead of being forced to live

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.373
as somebody don't feel they are.

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:59.040
- [Mark] What do you think
the most misunderstood part

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.240
of being transgender is?

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:04.720
You must get all kinds
of different reactions,

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:05.553
violent reactions.

00:09:05.553 --> 00:09:10.503
- The most wrong thinking
being transgender is

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.900
that it's a mental problem.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:17.258
Over in Europe, they
actually have studies,

00:09:17.258 --> 00:09:22.230
that pre-hrt and everything else.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.950
They used to only be
able to do it by optopsy

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:26.180
and they weren't sure

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:29.370
whether the hormones
change the brain or not,

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:32.993
but there's different
site areas of the brain.

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:42.190
A trans individual matches
perfectly for female like me,

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.860
would match perfectly for female

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:50.160
and trans males match a male,

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.923
especially in the gray and
white area of the brain,

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.003
for matter wise,

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.660
there's all sorts of studies done

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:05.393
like at Oxford and European
countries that have proven that.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.993
I just wish that a lot of
this would get out more to,

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.013
show and also there's studies where,

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:24.483
they asked five-year-old kids questions,

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:29.530
about how they feel as a gender

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:32.810
and the trans individual answer exactly

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:35.520
the way a female would
answer the questions.

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:38.540
There's no right or wrong
way to answer the questions

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:42.655
and the trans man answer, a boy answers

00:10:42.655 --> 00:10:45.322
the same way a boy would answer,

00:10:51.182 --> 00:10:55.220
and that kind of shows that
it's more in the brain,

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:58.823
than it is anything else.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:03.183
The most common misconception is,

00:11:05.584 --> 00:11:10.010
that we're mentally ill
or that we're confused,

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:13.600
or we don't know what we are

00:11:21.323 --> 00:11:23.450
and if it would get out there more

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:29.130
on the studies, the hate might lessen.

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.630
- [Mark] Yeah, that'd be nice, right?

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.120
Do you have any family that
you stay in touch with?

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:35.440
- My mom and my sister,

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.230
my sister by

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:42.190
Facebook and my mom by phone.

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:44.050
- [Mark] This is your stepmom?

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.030
- My biological.
- [Mark] Your biological mom?

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:47.820
- I have a relationship with her,

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.610
even though I was in foster care.

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.120
- [Mark] I see.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.860
- And then I have a old foster mom,

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:59.763
the one that I lived next to
the ex governor of Montana,

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:03.543
that I stay in touch with too as well,

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.930
but they're all the way back in Montana.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:09.763
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:12:11.435 --> 00:12:14.150
Leanna, thank you so
much for talking to me.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:16.300
Good luck with everything,
getting housing.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:18.093
- Thank you.

00:12:18.093 --> 00:12:18.926
- [Mark] Thank you.

